<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea 3-yr yields hit new year high.</title>
<headline>South Korea 3-yr yields hit new year high.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year corporate bonds closed at a new year high on Thursday in thin trading due to heavy new issues, brokers said.</p>
<p>Three-month CD yields also rose on the back of frozen buying interests. But overnight call rates closed unchanged with banks sticking to daily routine deals, they said.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates end at 12.59 pct from Wednesday's 12.43</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs close at 13.70 pct from 13.50</p>
<p>* Overnight call average 13.00 pct from 13.00</p>
<p>-- JAE HUR (822) 727 5651</p>
